This confirms: CHEM 299's Monday sections are evening (7:30-8:50 PM) and morning (11:30 AM-12:20 PM) — not afternoon. So **CHEM 300: Department Colloquium** is the only graduate-level Chemistry course meeting on Monday afternoon in Winter 2023, scheduled 3:00–4:20 PM in STLC 111 (STLC = Sapp Lab for Chemistry), taught by T. Markland, running Jan 9 – Mar 17, 2023.

No sign-in, account creation, or personal data was required at any point — this is all publicly browsable.

ANSWER: {"answer": "Starting at stanford.edu, I navigated through Academics to Stanford's public course catalog (ExploreCourses, explorecourses.stanford.edu), selected the 2022-2023 academic year, searched the Chemistry (CHEM) subject, and filtered by Winter term, Graduate career level, Monday, and afternoon (2-5pm) time slot. Result: only one graduate chemistry course meets on Monday afternoons in Winter 2023 — CHEM 300: Department Colloquium (1 unit, required of graduate students, repeatable), taught by Prof. Thomas Markland. It met Mondays 3:00-4:20 PM in room STLC 111 (Sapp Lab for Chemistry), Jan 9 - Mar 17, 2023, with 138/225 students enrolled; notes indicate it's for all pre-TGR PhD candidates in chemistry (plus undergrads in Chem 190). Other graduate CHEM courses with Monday meetings that winter (CHEM 223 Advanced Organic Chemistry II, CHEM 273 Advanced Physical Chemistry, and CHEM 299 Teaching of Chemistry) met at other times of day (lunchtime 12:30-1:20pm, morning 11:30am-12:20pm, or evening 7:30-8:50pm), not in the afternoon. No sign-in or personal data was needed to browse this public schedule."}

